  "title": "Modi's SCO Summit Visit and India's Vision for a Peaceful Region",
  "summary": "Modi embarks on a two-nation tour to Uzbekistan and Kyrgyzstan to participate in the 26th SCO Summit, focusing on security, connectivity, and opportunity to advance India's vision for a region free from terrorism and separatism. The visit aims to strengthen India's strategic partnerships and deepen its engagement with Central Asia.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Modi will travel to Uzbekistan and Kyrgyzstan to participate in the 26th SCO Summit.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The summit emphasizes security, connectivity, and opportunity as key elements of India's vision for a peaceful region.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The visit is part of a broader effort to strengthen India's strategic partnerships and engage in civilizational connect with Central Asia.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
